Z||000000||JBGehling||03-14-2001||10:56 PM||||Whoever was asking about the absence of a fiero GTP kit car got me wondering why no-one has ever made a kit of the 89 Fiero GT yet?  I think the car looks awesome and think it would be really cool to have an "89" Fiero w/ an Olds Quad-4.<P>Josh<P>If anyone ever made a kit, I'd be more than happy to put it on my car  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">!||||reg||1
Z||000001||WKDFIRO||03-15-2001||02:36 AM||||Apparently there has been much talk about it and I remember seeing a very revealing early Pontiac marketing video about the next gen Fiero by Hulki himself with pieces being fastened on.<P>The one thing that sticks out in my mind was that the new body needed some extra support underneath for the rear clip. They seemed to be using the same chassis for the new Fiero as well. <P>Why nobody has done it yet...probably because unlike the Ferrari kits there really isn't anything that stand as a model for the new body panels...I understand it takes a lot of upfront money to build the molds for any body kit!<P>A tragedy none the less.||||reg||9
